-in-Focus program\\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nWhat is precision hematology?\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s214\",\"d1\",4856,5250,\"Genetic profiling\\nDrug-sensitivity testing\\nThis field brings together physicians, scientists, and other key stakeholders across preclinical, translational, and clinical research. Through this collaboration, precision hematology aims to:\\nAccelerate the discovery of new treatment strategies\\nRefine therapeutic decision-making\\nImprove outcomes for patients with blood cancers\\nOur program’s goals\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s215\",\"d1\",5250,5562,\"Our Precision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program is designed to promote innovative concepts for diagnostics and innovative clinical trial designs which will feed into the clinical application of precision hematology.\\nThe goal of the program is to create a European regulatory framework for precision hematology. \",\"document\",[]],[\"s216\",\"d1\",5562,5909,\"By increasing awareness and providing education, guidelines, and policies, we can improve access to:\\nDiagnostics\\nClinical research\\nTreatment in malignant hematology\\nUseful materials\\nEHA Position Paper on Personalized Treatment for Hematologic Diseases\\nPrecision Medicine in Hematology in 2021: Definitions, Tools, Perspectives, and Open Questions\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s217\",\"d1\",5909,6307,\"In Vitro Diagnostic Medical Devices Regulation (IVDR) Initiatives at EHA\\nPreceptorship meeting\\nTopic-in-Focus Research Grant\\nTopic-in-Focus Bilateral Collaborative Grant\\nPosition papers on HemaSphere\\nGuidelines\\nShare\\nTopics-in-Focus program\\nPrecision Hematology Topics-in-Focus program\\nHemoglobinopathies Topics-in-Focus program\\nJoin EHA\\nFull membership\\nJunior membership\\n60-day trial\\nGet involved\\n\",\"document\",[]],[\"s218\",\"d1\",6307,6587,\"Career development\\nScientific meetings\\nAbout us\\nMission and vision\\nJobs\\nSponsor EHA\\nContact us\\nFollow us\\nPrivacy statement\\nTerms 